],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSuppose that $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ are complex numbers such that \\[\\begin{aligned} xy &= -80 - 320i, \\\\ yz &=60, \\\\ zx &= -96 + 24i, \\end{aligned}\\]where $i^2 = -1.$ Compute $|x+y+z|.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"7d04b7c89238a1b495c6047ef89eb7803674bcbc1f7536dcc079b28b35c4de22"},"seconds":76.93914103507996,"seed":818069251792165579,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given equations involving the complex numbers \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\nxy = -80 - 320i,\n\\]\n\\[\nyz = 60,\n\\]\n\\[\nzx = -96 + 24i.\n\\]\n\nFirst, we find the product \\(xyz\\) by multiplying all three equations together:\n\n\\[\n(xy)(yz)(zx) = (-80 - 320i)(60)(-96 + 24i).\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n(xyz)^2 = (-80 - 320i)(60)(-96 + 24i).\n\\]\n\nWe first compute the product \\((-80 - 320i)(-96 + 24i)\\):\n\n\\[\n(-80 - 320i)(-96 + 24i) = (-80)(-96) + (-80)(24i) + (-320i)(-96) + (-320i)(24i).\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term individually:\n\n\\[\n(-80)(-96) = 7680,\n\\]\n\\[\n(-80)(24i) = -1920i,\n\\]\n\\[\n(-320i)(-96) = 30720i,\n\\]\n\\[\n(-320i)(24i) = -7680i^2 = 7680 \\quad \\text{(since \\(i^2 = -1\\))}.\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\n7680 - 1920i + 30720i + 7680 = 15360 + 28800i.\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n(xyz)^2 = 15360 + 28800i \\cdot 60 = 921600 + 1728000i.\n\\]\n\nWe now find the square root of \\(921600 + 1728000i\\). Let \\(xyz = a + bi\\), then:\n\n\\[\n(a + bi)^2 = 921600 + 1728000i.\n\\]\n\nEquating real and imaginary parts, we have:\n\n\\[\na^2 - b^2 = 921600,\n\\]\n\\[\n2ab = 1728000.\n\\]\n\nFrom \\(2ab = 1728000\\), we get \\(ab = 864000\\). We solve the system of equations by substitution or trial and error. Let's try \\(a = 1200\\) and \\(b = 720\\):\n\n\\[\n1200 \\cdot 720 = 864000,\n\\]\n\\[\n1200^2 - 720^2 = 1440000 - 518400 = 921600.\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(xyz = 1200 + 720i\\).\n\nNext, we find \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) individually. Using \\(xy = -80 - 320i\\) and \\(yz = 60\\), we express \\(x\\) and \\(z\\) in terms of \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-80 - 320i}{y}, \\quad z = \\frac{60}{y}.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting into \\(zx = -96 + 24i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{-80 - 320i}{y}\\right) \\left(\\frac{60}{y}\\right) = -96 + 24i,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{60(-80 - 320i)}{y^2} = -96 + 24i,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{-4800 - 19200i}{y^2} = -96 + 24i.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(y^2 = \\frac{-4800 - 19200i}{-96 + 24i}\\):\n\n\\[\ny^2 = 50 + 200i,\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\sqrt{50 + 200i}.\n\\]\n\nUsing the same method as before, we find \\(y = 10 + 20i\\), then:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-80 - 320i}{10 + 20i} = -16,\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\frac{60}{10 + 20i} = 2 - 4i.\n\\]\n\nFinally, we compute \\(|x + y + z|\\):\n\n\\[\nx + y + z = -16 + (10 + 20i) + (2 - 4i) = -4 + 16i,\n\\]\n\\[\n|x + y + z| = \\sqrt{(-4)^2 + 16^2} = \\sqrt{16 + 256} = \\sqrt{272} = 4\\sqrt{17}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4\\sqrt{17}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{4\\sqrt{17}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
